# Building Atrinik server

Install CMake 3.21 or newer, Ninja, a C17 compiler, Flex, MiniUPnPc,
libcurl, OpenSSL, zlib, libgd, Python development headers, and Check. Then run:

```sh
python3 tools/dependencies.py sync
cmake --preset linux-debug
cmake --build --preset linux-debug
ctest --preset linux-debug
```

The first configure downloads the exact protocol and libatrinik source release
archives recorded in `cmake/dependencies.lock.json` and verifies their SHA-256
digests. Runtime content and server resources are installed from the release
archives recorded in `dependencies.lock.json`.

CMake's `FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_ATRINIK_PROTOCOL` and
`FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_LIBATRINIK` overrides support coordinated local work.

